<title>USA: TCI files shelf of $500 mln preferred.</title>
<headline>TCI files shelf of $500 mln preferred.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>TCI Communications Inc. filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission for a shelf offering of up to $500 million of preferred securities.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the sale will be invested in subordinated debt securities of the company, it said. Proceeds from the sale of the debt securities will be used to repay indebtedness outstanding under its commercial paper program, it said.</p>
<p>Lehman Brothers and Merrill Lynch &amp; Co. will underwrite the offering, the company said.</p>
</text>
